# The debug segment mesh is rewritten on every mortar rebuild, so the gold is the mesh from the
# final residual evaluation, i.e. whichever iterate Newton stops on. At nl_abs_tol = 1e-8 (see the
# "delaunay" cli_args comment in ../tests for why that floor is needed) that iterate's nodal
# coordinates can disagree between platforms by ~1e-6, marginally above exodiff's fixed 1e-6
# absolute coordinate tolerance (ED_SystemInterface.h's default coord_tol). That tolerance governs
# node matching and the post-mapping coordinate check; neither rel_err nor abs_zero can reach it,
# since those only feed variable comparisons -- only a COORDINATES line in a custom_cmp file can.
# These segment-mesh files carry zero variables and zero time steps, so a COORDINATES-only cmp
# loses no other comparison.
COORDINATES absolute 1.e-5
